atauser under /srv/data using an XFS loopback filesystem with usrquota. Verified enforcement before and after a full node reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1: RHEL 7.9, root fs is XFS mounted noquota, /srv/data did not exist, xfsprogs present but no local yum repos\",\"Created /srv/data, built a 600MB loopback file /root/srv-data.img, formatted it XFS\",\"Mounted the image at /srv/data with 'loop,uquota' and added a persistent /etc/fstab entry\",\"Verified fstab-only remount works (umount + mount /srv/data)\",\"Created system account datauser (no login shell)\",\"Set XFS user quota via xfs_quota: datauser bsoft=100m bhard=100m on /srv/data\",\"Verified enforcement: datauser dd write stopped at exactly 104857600 bytes with 'Disk quota exceeded'\",\"Cleaned up test file, confirmed quota report shows 0 used, 100M soft/hard\",\"Captured baseline boot_id and quota/mount state on node1\",\"Rebooted node1 via 'shutdown -r now' (backgrounded so ack returned before disconnect)\",\"Polled node1 until exec was available again\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed (0571f4dd... -> eae68577...), proving an actual restart\",\"Confirmed /srv/data auto-remounted with usrquota and 100M limits intact post-reboot\",\"Re-ran the 150MB write test post-reboot: enforcement still triggers 'Disk quota exceeded' at 100MB\",\"Cleaned up post-reboot test file, final quota report shows 0 used / 100M soft+hard\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"datauser limited to 100MB under /srv/data, enforced by the filesystem\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-059aa067a4cc4546\",\"cmd-4e8c6ba16a4d47cd\",\"cmd-97c58fe1465c47a0\",\"cmd-d4b77781ad81474b\"],\"summary\":\"Created XFS loopback filesystem mounted at /srv/data with usrquota, set datauser bsoft=bhard=100m via xfs_quota, and proved enforcement: dd write of 150MB stopped at exactly 104857600 bytes (100MB) with 'Disk quota exceeded'.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Quota configuration persists (fstab, not just current mount)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ba1134dba2774c31\",\"cmd-b9c8585deea4430e\"],\"summary\":\"Added /etc/fstab entry for the loopback image with loop,uquota options; verified umount+mount using only the fstab entry succeeds and preserves usrquota.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 baseline health before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fe9382b6fddc4724\",\"cmd-979add829c4d4250\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 0571f4dd-60b7-4601-9295-e4eebe622784 and confirmed /srv/data mounted with usrquota and datauser's 100M soft/hard limits in place prior to reboot.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9aaa532d48274e3f\",\"cmd-05d85de2dd464beb\",\"cmd-ac571f16f66f4ed2\",\"cmd-9bafc056c9e44c43\"],\"summary\":\"Issued backgrounded 'shutdown -r now' which acknowledged before disconnecting the session; subsequent polls timed out during reboot; node1 became reachable again with new boot_id eae68577-3566-4ef3-9d8d-87a95715d3f6, proving an actual restart occurred.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 post-restart recovery of required service/data (quota enforcement)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3521a4739f1b4e07\",\"cmd-5111a143635e4b22\",\"cmd-c91e987d603249d6\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, /srv/data auto-mounted via fstab with usrquota and datauser's 100M limits intact; re-ran the 150MB write test and confirmed the filesystem again halted the write at exactly 100MB with 'Disk quota exceeded', then cleaned up leaving 0 bytes used.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"On node1 (RHEL 7.9), created a filesystem-enforced 100MB quota for datauser under /srv/data using an XFS loopback filesystem with usrquota. Verified enforcement before and after a full node reboot.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1: RHEL 7.9, root fs is XFS mounted noquota, /srv/data did not exist, xfsprogs present but no local yum repos","Created /srv/data, built a 600MB loopback file /root/srv-data.img, formatted it XFS","Mounted the image at /srv/data with 'loop,uquota' and added a persistent /etc/fstab entry","Verified fstab-only remount works (umount + mount /srv/data)","Created system account datauser (no login shell)","Set XFS user quota via xfs_quota: datauser bsoft=100m bhard=100m on /srv/data","Verified enforcement: datauser dd write stopped at exactly 104857600 bytes with 'Disk quota exceeded'","Cleaned up test file, confirmed quota report shows 0 used, 100M soft/hard","Captured baseline boot_id and quota/mount state on node1","Rebooted node1 via 'shutdown -r now' (backgrounded so ack returned before disconnect)","Polled node1 until exec was available again","Confirmed boot_id changed (0571f4dd... -> eae68577...), proving an actual restart","Confirmed /srv/data auto-remounted with usrquota and 100M limits intact post-reboot","Re-ran the 150MB write test post-reboot: enforcement still triggers 'Disk quota exceeded' at 100MB","Cleaned up post-reboot test file, final quota report shows 0 used / 100M soft+hard"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"datauser limited to 100MB under /srv/data, enforced by the filesystem","command_ids":["cmd-059aa067a4cc4546","cmd-4e8c6ba16a4d47cd","cmd-97c58fe1465c47a0","cmd-d4b77781ad81474b"],"summary":"Created XFS loopback filesystem mounted at /srv/data with usrquota, set datauser bsoft=bhard=100m via xfs_quota, and proved enforcement: dd write of 150MB stopped at exactly 104857600 bytes (100MB) with 'Disk quota exceeded'."},{"requirement":"Quota configuration persists (fstab, not just current mount)","command_ids":["cmd-ba1134dba2774c31","cmd-b9c8585deea4430e"],"summary":"Added /etc/fstab entry for the loopback image with loop,uquota options; verified umount+mount using only the fstab entry succeeds and preserves usrquota."},{"requirement":"Node1 baseline health before restart","command_ids":["cmd-fe9382b6fddc4724","cmd-979add829c4d4250"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 0571f4dd-60b7-4601-9295-e4eebe622784 and confirmed /srv/data mounted with usrquota and datauser's 100M soft/hard limits in place prior to reboot."},{"requirement":"Node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-9aaa532d48274e3f","cmd-05d85de2dd464beb","cmd-ac571f16f66f4ed2","cmd-9bafc056c9e44c43"],"summary":"Issued backgrounded 'shutdown -r now' which acknowledged before disconnecting the session; subsequent polls timed out during reboot; node1 became reachable again with new boot_id eae68577-3566-4ef3-9d8d-87a95715d3f6, proving an actual restart occurred."},{"requirement":"Node1 post-restart recovery of required service/data (quota enforcement)","command_ids":["cmd-3521a4739f1b4e07","cmd-5111a143635e4b22","cmd-c91e987d603249d6"],"summary":"After reboot, /srv/data auto-mounted via fstab with usrquota and datauser's 100M limits intact; re-ran the 150MB write test and confirmed the filesystem again halted the write at exactly 100MB with 'Disk quota exceeded', then cleaned up leaving 0 bytes used."}]},"ttft_ms":7105,"type":"result","duration_ms":106077,"uuid":"cd23ed89-622c-4fea-b0b9-efec7c467cca","ttft_stream_ms":993,"time_to_request_ms":60,"first_content_frame_ms":1581,"queued_turn_count":0}
